{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And they judged.</b> They judged the nation." "<b>They would bring.</b> They would bring." "<b>They shall judge themselves.</b> Like ״they shall judge,״ and likewise ״you shall not pass״ (Ruth 2) — like ״you shall not pass.״ And its Targum is: they judged. The upper verses are in the imperative mood — therefore they are translated: let them judge, let them bring, let them judge. But these verses are in the language of action."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:00.535814055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}